/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 540 0 R
/E (Uniform Weighting Enhances Quality: Discarding variational lower bound terms in favor of uniform weighting significantly improves sample quality. This approach penalizes reconstruction errors equally across all time steps, whereas standard weighting fails to sufficiently penalize errors at high noise levels. )
/Pg 7 0 R
/K [0 1]
>>
endobj
288 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 541 0 R
/E (Guidance Scale Trade-off: While classifier guidance directs generation toward specific classes, a high guidance scale    forces the model to focus only on the most probable features. This reduces intra-class diversity and degrades FID scores, whereas a balanced scale \(           \) optimizes both quality and diversity.)
/Pg 7 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
289 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 542 0 R
/E (Learned Variance Boosts Likelihood: Incorporating learned variance enhances NLL scores without modifying the model architecture or degrading sample quality \(FID\).)
/Pg 7 0 R
/K [3]
>>
